.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-BUILD-MONITOR 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-build-monitor
.Nd show, unmissably, that a new install is still building, and when it is safe to restart
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A kldload install reaches a usable desktop long before it has finished:
first boot fetches models and builds kernel modules, and the automatic
deployment then builds golden images and a cluster, with up to six hours
allowed.
.Nm
shows a BUILDING banner with the current phase, a checklist of every
phase planned, the time so far and the log that is moving, refreshed
every two seconds; then a closing banner, READY or finished with phases
that did not complete.
The window closing is the signal that a restart is safe.
It opens from its icon.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the header comment and exit 0.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kldload-autodeploy 8 ,
.Xr kldload-firstboot 8 ,
.Xr kldload-install-status 8
